course: dictionary
lesson: 9118
title: Blends: smoke plus fog
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blend is a new word made by joining parts of two other words. «Smog» is a blend of "smoke" and "fog", so it names something that is a bit of both: a dirty haze over a city.
explain: Context gives the clues. «Smog is a dirty haze of smoke and car fumes that builds up in still air.» Dirty, haze, smoke and still air all point to foggy, polluted air. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Smog is a dirty, smoky, foggy air..." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Smog is not just a word for a grey day. It is air pollution, and it makes breathing hard, especially for people with asthma. Cleaner cars and fuels have helped many cities' air become clearer.
fact: A blend joins parts of two words: brunch (breakfast + lunch), smog (smoke + fog) and motel (motor + hotel).
fact: «Smog» means dirty, smoky, foggy air over a city, caused by pollution from cars, factories and fires.
fact: The Great Smog of London killed thousands of people and led to clean air laws.
fact: Many big cities today issue smog warnings, so people know to take care when the air is bad.
fact: Hangry (hungry + angry) is a blend too, and it is now in major dictionaries.
exercise: Which two words were joined to make «smog»? | *smoke and fog | hungry and angry | breakfast and lunch | motor and hotel
exercise: «Smog is a dirty haze of smoke and car fumes that builds up in still air.» What is smog? | A type of fog at sea | *Dirty, foggy air over a city | A clean, sunny sky | A kind of car
exercise: Which word is a blend, made from parts of two words? | *brunch | garden | table | running
test: Smog makes breathing hard, especially for people with which condition? | people who swim | people who sing | *asthma | people who sleep late
test: The word «motel» is a blend. Which two words does it join? | *motor and hotel | hungry and angry | breakfast and lunch | smoke and fog
exam: Why is «smog» called a blend? | It is a word meaning a happy, sunny day | It is a word for a cloud | It is a longer form of fog | *It is a new word made from parts of smoke and fog
